#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087441 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b9ef325-2358-5041-8a8d-b459e8ed9f09" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "4f4be86f-5a12-5fdf-b98e-2095b1faae8f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4499" :question/problem "Using the method of direct verification, determine whether the matrix $B$ is the inverse of $A$, where\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "We must check whether\n\n$$\nAB = BA = I_2\n$$\n\nComputing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= I_{2}.✓\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $BA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nBA &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= I_{2}.✓\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B = A^{-1}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087442 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a75c67e5-3469-5730-9181-54df4ec6d5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a Larger Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "7ab2814b-dc93-569b-bdd6-618880da6e2c" :question/math-academy-id "e-4500" :question/problem "Using the method of direct verification, determine whether the matrix $B$ is the inverse of $A$, where\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "First, we check whether\n\n$$\nAB = BA = I_3\n$$\n\nComputing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= I_{3}.✓\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $BA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nBA &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= I_{3}.✓\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B = A^{-1}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087925 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b9ef325-2358-5041-8a8d-b459e8ed9f09" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0b84fae-6548-5fa8-8480-09519247f743" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084562} {:answer/id #uuid "b38a1764-56d4-530f-b0b5-537ebc66b8d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084563} {:answer/id #uuid "bb8137a8-d8ed-517c-82c3-bae667437088" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084564} {:answer/id #uuid "1743a9e4-194f-50ff-8567-edce28c3658b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084565} {:answer/id #uuid "5bb8f1aa-ef04-57d6-a556-791c248d4155" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084566}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1743a9e4-194f-50ff-8567-edce28c3658b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084565} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e3eabdb-8b0a-57e8-91b8-80a42fbb99cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084561}] :question/id #uuid "b6c389a4-1252-5fbd-bc91-0070ca92b082" :question/math-academy-id "q-11640" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n$B = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}, D = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $BC = CB = I_{2}$\n2. $BD = DB = I_{2}$\n3. $D = B^{-1}$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088311 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a75c67e5-3469-5730-9181-54df4ec6d5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a Larger Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a37de327-3367-5d19-86dd-0103f21a1e16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086797} {:answer/id #uuid "c8a8cbdd-712e-5a0d-a44c-909ff99a6b9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086798} {:answer/id #uuid "ea0b3705-5098-5c30-9a93-fdd5856796b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086799} {:answer/id #uuid "6bf7759a-66b8-536f-816c-2b1a382a35f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086800} {:answer/id #uuid "6ff046a9-73c1-5d38-8410-dee1f2e6533a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086801}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea0b3705-5098-5c30-9a93-fdd5856796b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086799} :answer-field/id #uuid "99b0b0b7-15a8-54bb-b710-ce52d4ef20d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086796}] :question/id #uuid "a9b82ee6-5237-523c-b3cf-ec1dac0a4451" :question/math-academy-id "q-7913" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & 6\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & 6\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -6\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $AB = BA = I_{4}$\n2. $AC = CA = I_{4}$\n3. $B = A^{-1}$"}]}
